      "side": 1,
      "message": "This only works for modules which have a registered module type associated with a ModuleFactory (and probably only for factories which do not use a dynamically declared factory function; i.e. only for those which have a static function declaration).\n\nSo there are some modules which still have an unlabeled type in the json-module-graph. This could be remedied by registering those factories with a module type, or by changing the LoadHookContext.CreateModule API such that all callers have to explicitly pass a module type.\n\nI think the latter option is worse because it:\n1) requires many changes across the codebase, and\n2) requires me to either to hardcode module types in many different code locations, or create a global listing of module types that could be reused in different places: e.g.\n```\nvar (\n    JavaImportModuleType \u003d \"java_import\",\n    ...\n)\n```",
      "revId": "b5a17a12556a9747d3d7439067fb6ea8b5847261",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
